[{:db/id 17592186374407 :question/problem "![](images/79/79df94546a6fafcd66f8733622e8e9d8c37d29c24cb99378eba141610a8fdc8a.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,x-1\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=x-1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<x-1\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that some points in our set lie *on* the line. We include these points by changing the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\le x-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le x-1\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186383633 :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2591e9da960008980cf96184975ef19713735814183a97ca8c8f784536fced5.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x-3\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,x+4\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x-3$ and *below* the line $y=x+4.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x-3,\\,y<x+4.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x-3<y<x+4.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=-x-3$ and $y=x+4$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\n-x-3\\le y\\le x+4\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x-3\\le y\\le x+4\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287727 :question/problem "![](images/6a/6affe267a93d1dab16de3dc153fddbdb165bab831790f7387dcbd29354ebb63a.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *below* the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the curve is dashed), the inequality is strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287729 :question/problem "![](images/c6/c670ed592fc32716596aae470911923627d1c6861a75a1c885659d09005e0a84.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$36$\n\n$\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=2$ and vertical radius $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *inside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point inside the region, say, $(0,0).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n9(0)^{2}+4(0)^{2}\\,<\\,36.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287190 :answer-field/correct "answer-54412ad1-cdc0-5927-bece-9ef714771a8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-54412ad1-cdc0-5927-bece-9ef714771a8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54412ad1-cdc0-5927-bece-9ef714771a8b" :answer/id #uuid "54412ad1-cdc0-5927-bece-9ef714771a8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287779 :question/problem "![](images/01/010d4befaa2bd2142cf63010f79f071df331bb6394eb65e4f883752cb04a2cb4.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,-x+1\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x+1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x+1\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that some points in our set lie *on* the line. We include these points by changing the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge -x+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -x+1\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-cc2eec70-1647-5419-a327-f6c1951358dd" :activity/id #uuid "cc2eec70-1647-5419-a327-f6c1951358dd" :activity/title "Describing Planar Regions Using Set-Builder Notation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051063 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-1cdff818-5e0c-5b45-b6f2-7455eaaf1808" "step-9354686a-acc6-5fa4-8bd7-5f500db8971a" "step-f5432599-bb88-543b-8395-a965094cbe30" "step-fcf0ef42-6ecb-558a-9e0e-218f1cbed866" "step-99cbd0ca-b0f9-5db2-8595-6cf285bf96fb"] :activity/first-step "step-1cdff818-5e0c-5b45-b6f2-7455eaaf1808" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-1cdff818-5e0c-5b45-b6f2-7455eaaf1808" :step/id #uuid "1cdff818-5e0c-5b45-b6f2-7455eaaf1808" :step/content 17592186374407 :step/next "step-9354686a-acc6-5fa4-8bd7-5f500db8971a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9354686a-acc6-5fa4-8bd7-5f500db8971a" :step/id #uuid "9354686a-acc6-5fa4-8bd7-5f500db8971a" :step/content 17592186383633 :step/next "step-f5432599-bb88-543b-8395-a965094cbe30" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f5432599-bb88-543b-8395-a965094cbe30" :step/id #uuid "f5432599-bb88-543b-8395-a965094cbe30" :step/content 17592186287727 :step/next "step-fcf0ef42-6ecb-558a-9e0e-218f1cbed866" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fcf0ef42-6ecb-558a-9e0e-218f1cbed866" :step/id #uuid "fcf0ef42-6ecb-558a-9e0e-218f1cbed866" :step/content 17592186287729 :step/next "step-99cbd0ca-b0f9-5db2-8595-6cf285bf96fb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-99cbd0ca-b0f9-5db2-8595-6cf285bf96fb" :step/id #uuid "99cbd0ca-b0f9-5db2-8595-6cf285bf96fb" :step/content 17592186287779 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
